>Science.</source> <volume>313</volume>:<fpage>1960</fpage>&#x02013;1964.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17008531</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib23"><label>23</label><citation citation-type="journal">Koebel, C.M., W. Vermi, J.B. Swann, N. Zerafa, S.J. Rodig, L.J. Old, M.J. Smyth, and R.D. Schreiber. <year>2007</year>. Adaptive immunity maintains occult cancer in an equilibrium state. <source>Nature.</source> <volume>450</volume>:<fpage>903</fpage>&#x02013;907.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18026089</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib24"><label>24</label><citation citation-type="journal">Langowski, J.L., X. Zhang, L. Wu, J.D. Mattson, T. Chen, K. Smith, B. Basham, T. McClanahan, R.A. Kastelein, and M. Oft. <year>2006</year>. IL-23 promotes tumor incidence and growth. <source>Nature.</source> <volume>442</volume>:<fpage>461</fpage>&#x02013;465.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16688182</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib25"><label>25</label><citation citation-type="journal">Bettelli, E., M. Oukka, and V.K. Kuchroo. <year>2007</year>. T(H)-17 cells in the circle of immunity and autoimmunity. <source>Nat. Immunol.</source> <volume>8</volume>:<fpage>345</fpage>&#x02013;350.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17375096</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>